22. 🔐 R6.5 INVARIANTS

R6.5-I01
Anomaly SHALL mean deviation, not guilt.

R6.5-I02
Constitutional baselines SHALL be normatively anchored.

R6.5-I03
Statistical normality SHALL NOT establish authority.

R6.5-I04
Historical events SHALL be evaluated against the
baseline valid at their occurrence time.

R6.5-I05
Baseline changes SHALL be versioned and append-only.

R6.5-I06
Anomalies SHALL preserve provenance.

R6.5-I07
Anomaly confidence SHALL remain distinct from proof.

R6.5-I08
Unknown SHALL remain an explicit valid state.

R6.5-I09
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge observations
AND baselines.

R6.5-I10
TRIAS SHALL be able to validate baseline legitimacy.

R6.5-I11
Anomaly detection SHALL NOT directly mutate
constitutional state.

R6.5-I12
Resolved anomalies SHALL remain historically observable.


