En:

> Op welke gegevens baseerde het model zich?




---

24. 🔐 NO MODEL SOVEREIGNTY

De absolute regel:

MODEL OUTPUT
     ↓
RISK ASSESSMENT
     ↓
REVIEW

nooit:

MODEL OUTPUT
     ↓
AUTHORITY

Een AI kan dus zeggen:

> "Ik zie een mogelijk constitutioneel risico."



Maar niet:

> "Daarom heb ik constitutionele bevoegdheid."




---

25. 🔱 R6.6 INVARIANTS

R6.6-I01
Risk SHALL remain distinct from anomaly.

R6.6-I02
Risk SHALL remain distinct from proof.

R6.6-I03
Risk SHALL remain distinct from authority.

R6.6-I04
Risk assessments SHALL preserve provenance.

R6.6-I05
Risk confidence SHALL remain distinct from factual certainty.

R6.6-I06
Unknown likelihood SHALL remain a valid state.

R6.6-I07
Historical risk assessments SHALL remain immutable.

R6.6-I08
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge risk assumptions.

R6.6-I09
TRIAS SHALL independently evaluate risk validity.

R6.6-I10
Risk classification SHALL NOT directly execute intervention.

R6.6-I11
Response recommendations SHALL be proportional to assessed risk.

R6.6-I12
Automated models SHALL NOT acquire authority from their outputs.

R6.6-I13
Risk acceptance SHALL require authorized provenance.

R6.6-I14
Risk models SHALL be version-identifiable and auditable.


