27. 🔐 R6.9 INVARIANTS

R6.9-I01
Feedback SHALL preserve source provenance.

R6.9-I02
Observed outcomes SHALL remain distinct from expected outcomes.

R6.9-I03
Learning SHALL NOT create authority.

R6.9-I04
Recommendations SHALL remain distinct from decisions.

R6.9-I05
Corrections SHALL be explicitly classified by authority level.

R6.9-I06
Constitutional corrections SHALL require a separate authorized process.

R6.9-I07
Historical states SHALL remain immutable.

R6.9-I08
Every correction SHALL possess an evidence-backed rationale.

R6.9-I09
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge feedback and correction proposals.

R6.9-I10
TRIAS SHALL independently verify material corrections.

R6.9-I11
Correction effectiveness SHALL itself be observable.

R6.9-I12
Failed corrections SHALL remain historically visible.

R6.9-I13
Self-modification SHALL NOT bypass constitutional gates.

R6.9-I14
Model learning SHALL remain independently auditable.

R6.9-I15
No correction SHALL fabricate historical continuity.


