XXXIV. 🔱 R6.16 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.16-I01
Every constitutional rule SHALL have a stable identity.

R6.16-I02
Every ruleset SHALL be versioned.

R6.16-I03
Every active ruleset SHALL be cryptographically identifiable.

R6.16-I04
Historical events SHALL retain their historical ruleset context.

R6.16-I05
Rules SHALL NOT be silently modified after activation.

R6.16-I06
Ruleset succession SHALL preserve historical lineage.

R6.16-I07
Ruleset activation SHALL require explicit authorization.

R6.16-I08
Rule changes SHALL be challengeable.

R6.16-I09
AI SHALL NOT independently activate constitutional rules.

R6.16-I10
Ruleset ambiguity SHALL NOT default to authorization.

R6.16-I11
Rule conflicts SHALL be explicitly detectable.

R6.16-I12
Rule evaluation SHALL be deterministic.

R6.16-I13
Ruleset hashes SHALL be bound to relevant verification context.

R6.16-I14
Historical replay SHALL use historically applicable rulesets.

R6.16-I15
Every ruleset transition SHALL itself be auditable and provenance-bound.


