XXX. 🔱 R6.17 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.17-I01
Federation membership SHALL NOT confer constitutional authority.

R6.17-I02
Each member SHALL retain its own historical provenance.

R6.17-I03
Cross-domain actions SHALL have explicit authority.

R6.17-I04
Cross-domain events SHALL preserve source provenance.

R6.17-I05
Local history SHALL NOT be rewritten by federation processes.

R6.17-I06
Federated reconciliation SHALL preserve source watermarks.

R6.17-I07
Historical rulesets SHALL remain historically bound.

R6.17-I08
Conflicting valid states SHALL NOT be resolved by majority alone.

R6.17-I09
Federated uncertainty SHALL remain explicitly representable.

R6.17-I10
Provenance gaps SHALL NOT be converted into fabricated continuity.

R6.17-I11
Federation processes SHALL themselves produce evidence.

R6.17-I12
Federation results SHALL be independently verifiable.

R6.17-I13
AI SHALL NOT constitute federated constitutional authority.

R6.17-I14
FOOL SHALL retain unrestricted challenge capability.

R6.17-I15
Federation SHALL coordinate constitutional states without becoming an
unbounded constitutional authority.


