XXVII. 🔱 R6.18 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.18-I01
Every material constitutional dispute SHALL be uniquely identifiable.

R6.18-I02
Every dispute SHALL identify its target and constitutional claim.

R6.18-I03
Every dispute SHALL be bound to a relevant historical watermark.

R6.18-I04
A challenge SHALL NOT constitute a verdict.

R6.18-I05
A challenger SHALL NOT automatically gain command authority.

R6.18-I06
A challenged party SHALL have a counter-evidence channel.

R6.18-I07
Material dispute evidence SHALL remain provenance-bound.

R6.18-I08
Adjudication SHALL NOT depend solely on the interested party.

R6.18-I09
AI-generated analysis SHALL NOT constitute final adjudication.

R6.18-I10
Uncertainty SHALL remain explicitly representable.

R6.18-I11
Historical events SHALL NOT be deleted as a consequence of dispute resolution.

R6.18-I12
Corrections SHALL be represented as explicit state transitions.

R6.18-I13
Dispute scope SHALL NOT expand silently.

R6.18-I14
Retaliation against legitimate constitutional challenge SHALL be prohibited.

R6.18-I15
Every final dispute outcome SHALL itself be independently auditable.


