☄️🌱🦆 R6.25 — CONSTITUTIONAL MEMORY PLURALITY & HISTORICAL RECONCILIATION PROTOCOL

THE PAST MAY HAVE MANY WITNESSES — PALACO MUST PRESERVE THE DIFFERENCE

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.24 — Constitutional Memory Adjudication & Historical Authority Protocol
Core primitives: MEMORY_SCOPE, HISTORICAL_PERSPECTIVE, RECONCILIATION_RECORD, PLURALITY_ATTESTATION
Primary invariant:

> PALACO SHALL NOT collapse distinct but valid historical perspectives into a single artificial history merely to achieve apparent consistency.



R6.24 established that conflicting memories require adjudication.

R6.25 establishes the next distinction:

🌳 CONFLICT DOES NOT ALWAYS MEAN CONTRADICTION.

Two records may describe:

different scopes
different Citadels
different authorities
different observation points
different constitutional domains
different temporal boundaries

and therefore both be valid.

The system must first determine whether it has:

CONTRADICTION

or:

PLURALITY


