XIV. 🕰️ TEMPORAL GRAPH

R6.25 introduced partial temporal ordering.

R6.26 formalizes it.

A graph can encode:

A-W4 < A-W5
B-W2 < B-W3

without asserting:

A-W5 < B-W3

unless such ordering is proven.

Thus the historical graph may be a partially ordered directed acyclic graph where appropriate.

The architecture must not force every event into an artificial global sequence.


