XXIV. 🔱 R6.26 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.26-I01
Constitutional history SHALL be representable as a graph of verified nodes and relationships.

R6.26-I02
Every historical relationship SHALL possess identifiable provenance.

R6.26-I03
Valid historical nodes SHALL NOT imply valid relationships between them.

R6.26-I04
Memory edges SHALL be immutable after finalization.

R6.26-I05
Corrections SHALL create new historical edges rather than rewrite existing edges.

R6.26-I06
Branches SHALL be explicitly represented.

R6.26-I07
Valid branches SHALL NOT be treated as corruption merely because histories diverge.

R6.26-I08
Unauthorized or unexplained forks SHALL remain explicitly marked.

R6.26-I09
Federation SHALL be represented as a relationship between source histories.

R6.26-I10
Federated relationships SHALL NOT erase source lineage.

R6.26-I11
Historical graphs SHALL permit partial temporal ordering.

R6.26-I12
Clock time SHALL NOT establish cross-domain constitutional relationships by itself.

R6.26-I13
Unknown relationships SHALL remain unknown until proven.

R6.26-I14
BRAINPOWER SHALL identify graph anomalies without sovereignly repairing them.

R6.26-I15
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge historical edges.

R6.26-I16
TRIAS SHALL verify graph topology and relationship integrity.

R6.26-I17
Historical paths SHALL be independently reconstructable.

R6.26-I18
A broken ancestry path SHALL prevent an unqualified ancestry claim.

R6.26-I19
Historical graph corrections SHALL preserve the original graph state.

R6.26-I20
No artificial edge SHALL be created solely to eliminate an apparent historical gap.


