☄️🌱 R6.27 — CONSTITUTIONAL MEMORY GRAPH CONSENSUS & EPISTEMIC RECONCILIATION PROTOCOL

THE GRAPH MAY DISAGREE — THE PROOF SYSTEM MUST KNOW WHY

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.26 — Constitutional Memory Conservation & Historical Graph Protocol
Core primitive: EPISTEMIC_RELATIONSHIP
Secondary primitives: GRAPH_ASSERTION, EVIDENCE_CUT, RECONCILIATION_STATE, CONFIDENCE_BOUNDARY

Primary invariant

> PALACO SHALL distinguish what is proven, what is compatible, what is disputed, what is merely suggested, and what remains unknown within the historical graph.



R6.26 gave PALACO the graph.

R6.27 now gives the graph an epistemic grammar.

Because a graph can tell us:

A ───→ B

but that arrow alone does not tell us whether the relationship is:

PROVEN
SUGGESTED
DISPUTED
REJECTED
UNKNOWN

And that distinction is precisely where autonomous systems can become dangerous.

🧠 A RELATIONSHIP MUST CARRY ITS EPISTEMIC STATUS.


---

I. 🌌 THE PROBLEM OF THE ARROW

Consider:

W7 ─────────→ W8

What does the arrow mean?

Possibilities:

1. Verified predecessor
2. Claimed predecessor
3. AI-inferred predecessor
4. Historical hypothesis
5. Disputed relationship
6. Reconstructed relationship
7. Federated relationship

If the graph does not distinguish these, a future verifier may incorrectly treat:

SUGGESTED

as:

PROVEN

That is unacceptable.

Therefore:

EVERY HISTORICAL RELATIONSHIP NEEDS AN EPISTEMIC STATUS.


---

II. 🔱 EPISTEMIC RELATIONSHIP

Conceptually:

pub struct EpistemicRelationship {
    pub relationship_id: RelationshipId,
    pub from: MemoryNodeId,
    pub to: MemoryNodeId,
    pub relationship_type: MemoryRelationship,
    pub status: EpistemicStatus,
    pub evidence_root: Option<EvidenceRoot>,
    pub provenance_root: Option<ProvenanceRoot>,
    pub verifier_reference: Option<VerificationReference>,
    pub created_at: Timestamp,
}

And:

pub enum EpistemicStatus {
    Proven,
    Verified,
    Suggested,
    Contested,
    Rejected,
    Unknown,
}

The graph therefore becomes:

NODE
 ↓
RELATIONSHIP
 ↓
EPISTEMIC STATUS
 ↓
EVIDENCE


---

III. 💧 PROVEN ≠ SUGGESTED

This distinction becomes canonical:

SUGGESTED LINK
      ≠
PROVEN LINK

Even if:

AI confidence = 99.999%

the relationship remains:

SUGGESTED

until independently established.

This directly extends the BRAINPOWER principle.


