VII. 🌳 COMPATIBILITY IS NOT IDENTITY

Two histories may be compatible without being identical.

For example:

A-W7 → A-W8

and:

B-W3 → B-W4

may describe different domains but remain compatible under a federation.

Thus:

COMPATIBLE

does not mean:

SAME HISTORY

This distinction prevents silent historical collapse.


