XIII. 🕰️ EPISTEMIC TIME

A relationship has at least two relevant times:

HISTORICAL_TIME

and:

KNOWLEDGE_TIME

For example:

EVENT HAPPENED:
2025

PROVEN:
2026

Those are not the same timestamp.

Therefore:

WHEN SOMETHING HAPPENED ≠ WHEN PALACO ESTABLISHED THAT IT COULD BE PROVEN.

This is an extremely important forensic distinction.


