---

XXI. ☄️ THE EPISTEMIC LEDGER

R6.27 effectively creates a second layer of memory:

HISTORICAL MEMORY
                 │
                 ▼
          WHAT HAPPENED
                 │
                 ▼
          EPISTEMIC MEMORY
                 │
                 ▼
        WHAT WE CAN PROVE
                 │
                 ▼
        WHAT WE CURRENTLY KNOW

And those layers must remain distinct.


---

XXII. 🔱 R6.27 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.27-I01
Every historical relationship SHALL possess an explicit epistemic status.

R6.27-I02
Suggested relationships SHALL NOT be treated as proven relationships.

R6.27-I03
AI-generated hypotheses SHALL remain epistemically non-authoritative until independently verified.

R6.27-I04
TRIAS SHALL control promotion from suggested to verified status.

R6.27-I05
Epistemic status transitions SHALL be historically recorded.

R6.27-I06
Rejected claims SHALL remain discoverable.

R6.27-I07
Contested claims SHALL remain explicitly contested.

R6.27-I08
Compatibility SHALL NOT imply identity.

R6.27-I09
