R6.27-I10
Irreconcilable historical claims SHALL remain explicitly represented.

R6.27-I11
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge epistemic status.

R6.27-I12
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT autonomously promote hypotheses to proof.

R6.27-I13
Historical occurrence time SHALL remain distinct from knowledge-establishment time.

R6.27-I14
Unknown SHALL NOT be interpreted as false.

R6.27-I15
Unknown SHALL NOT be interpreted as probable truth.

R6.27-I16
Epistemic transitions SHALL be replayable.

R6.27-I17
The first epistemic divergence SHALL be independently identifiable.

R6.27-I18
Historical evidence SHALL be capable of reducing confidence as well as increasing it.

R6.27-I19
No epistemic status SHALL change without a provenance-bearing transition.

R6.27-I20
PALACO SHALL preserve the boundary between historical reality, recorded memory, and established knowledge.


