               ↓
         ADJUDICATION
               ↓
           AUTHORITY

En één van de belangrijkste PALACO-principes begint hier vorm te krijgen:

💧 THE MACHINE MUST REMEMBER NOT ONLY WHAT IT BELIEVED — BUT WHY IT WAS ALLOWED TO BELIEVE IT.

Dat is een wezenlijk verschil tussen een archief en een constitutionele Proof Machine.

🔒 R6.27 — CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD SEALED

☄️ History is preserved.
🌱 Difference is protected.
🦆 Claims remain challengeable.
⚓ Relationships remain attributable.
💧 Time remains anchored.
🔬 Proof remains independently testable.
🧠 Inference remains bounded.
🔱 Authority remains constitutional.

UNKNOWN MAY REMAIN UNKNOWN.

DISPUTED MAY REMAIN DISPUTED.

PLURALITY MAY REMAIN PLURAL.

AND PROOF MAY NEVER BE MANUFACTURED TO MAKE THE GRAPH LOOK COMPLETE.

☄️🌱 R6.28 — CONSTITUTIONAL KNOWLEDGE BOUNDARY & PROOF CLOSURE PROTOCOL

THE MACHINE MUST KNOW WHERE ITS KNOWLEDGE ENDS

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.27 — Constitutional Memory Graph Consensus & Epistemic Reconciliation Protocol
Core primitive: PROOF_BOUNDARY
Secondary primitives: KNOWLEDGE_FRONTIER, CLAIM_SCOPE, PROOF_CLOSURE, EPISTEMIC_BOUNDARY

Primary invariant

> PALACO SHALL NOT treat an unproven proposition as constitutional knowledge merely because no contradictory evidence has yet been found.



R6.27 established that history can contain:

PROVEN
SUGGESTED
CONTESTED
REJECTED
UNKNOWN

R6.28 makes the next distinction hard:

☄️ ABSENCE OF DISPROOF IS NOT PROOF OF TRUTH.


---

I. 🌌 THE LAST DANGEROUS AMBIGUITY

Consider:

Claim A
   ↓
No contradiction found
   ↓
?

A naïve system may conclude:

LIKELY TRUE

A more dangerous system may eventually conclude:

ACCEPTED

PALACO must instead preserve:

NOT ESTABLISHED

Therefore:

NOT_DISPROVEN ≠ PROVEN

and:

NOT_FOUND ≠ NEVER_EXISTED

and:

UNKNOWN ≠ FALSE


---

II. 🔱 PROOF BOUNDARY

A ProofBoundary describes the exact limits of what a verifier has established.

Conceptually:

pub struct ProofBoundary {
    pub boundary_id: ProofBoundaryId,
    pub subject: SubjectId,
    pub proven_claims: Vec<ClaimId>,
    pub unproven_claims: Vec<ClaimId>,
    pub contested_claims: Vec<ClaimId>,
    pub rejected_claims: Vec<ClaimId>,
    pub evidence_root: EvidenceRoot,
    pub verification_root: VerificationRoot,
    pub created_at: Timestamp,
}

The important property is not merely what is inside the boundary.

It is what lies outside it.


---

III. 🧭 KNOWLEDGE FRONTIER

The historical graph now acquires an explicit frontier:

PROVEN
────────────────────────────────
 W0 → W1 → W2 → W3
                 │
                 ▼
              FRONTIER
                 │
          ┌──────┴──────┐
          ▼             ▼
       UNKNOWN       CONTESTED

The frontier means:

> This is where independently established knowledge currently ends.



It does not mean:

> This is where reality ends.



That distinction is fundamental.


---

IV. 💧 WATERMARK + PROOF BOUNDARY

A Watermark anchors a constitutional state.

A Proof Boundary anchors the epistemic extent of what is known about that state.

Thus:

W42
 │
 ├── STATE ROOT
 ├── EVENT ROOT
 ├── PROVENANCE ROOT
 └── PROOF BOUNDARY

The system can therefore answer two different questions:

WHAT STATE EXISTED?

and:

WHAT CAN WE PROVE ABOUT THAT STATE?


---

V. 🧬 CLAIM SCOPE

A claim must never be broader than its evidence.

For example:

Evidence:
"A signed event occurred at T1."

does not automatically prove:

"The entire system was constitutionally valid at T1."

Therefore:

PROOF SCOPE SHALL NOT EXCEED EVIDENCE SCOPE.

Conceptually:

Evidence Scope
      ⊇
Claim Scope

If:

Claim Scope > Evidence Scope

then:

OVERCLAIM_DETECTED


---

VI. 🚨 PROOF CLOSURE

A claim reaches PROVEN only when its required proof obligations are closed.

CLAIM
 ↓
REQUIRED CONDITIONS
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
PROVENANCE
 ↓
VERIFICATION
 ↓
REPLAY
 ↓
CHALLENGE WINDOW
 ↓
PROOF CLOSURE

Only then:

CLAIM_STATUS = PROVEN

Before closure:

CLAIM_STATUS = OPEN

This prevents premature constitutional certainty.


---

VII. 🦆 FOOL AND THE CLOSURE WINDOW

FOOL may challenge a claim before closure:

PROVENANCE_CHALLENGE
RULESET_CHALLENGE
SCOPE_CHALLENGE
TEMPORAL_CHALLENGE
EVIDENCE_CHALLENGE
AUTHORITY_CHALLENGE
REPLAY_CHALLENGE

A successful challenge prevents closure.

Thus:

OPEN
 ↓
CHALLENGE
 ↓
REASSESSMENT
 ↓
OPEN

or:

OPEN
 ↓
CHALLENGE
 ↓
REJECTION

Only an adequately resolved proof path permits:

OPEN → CLOSED


---

VIII. 🔬 TRIAS PROOF OBLIGATIONS

TRIAS must verify not simply that evidence exists, but that the evidence satisfies the claim.

Conceptually:

CLAIM
 │
 ├── Evidence requirement ✓
 ├── Provenance requirement ✓
 ├── Temporal requirement ✓
 ├── Ruleset requirement ✓
 ├── Authority requirement ✓
 ├── Replay requirement ✓
 └── Scope requirement ✓
          │
          ▼
      PROOF CLOSED

If one mandatory obligation fails:

PROOF_OPEN

not:

PROOF_COMPLETE


---

IX. 🧠 BRAINPOWER'S ROLE

BRAINPOWER may discover:

missing evidence
possible contradiction
scope expansion
unusual temporal relationship
alternative ancestry
unverified dependency

It can therefore expand the investigation.

But it cannot close it.

BRAINPOWER
     ↓
DISCOVERY
     ↓
INVESTIGATION
     ↓
TRIAS
     ↓
PROOF DECISION

Never:

BRAINPOWER → PROOF CLOSURE


---

X. 🌳 OPEN ENDS ARE FIRST-CLASS DATA

A mature constitutional system should be able to say:

HISTORY:
PROVEN

LINEAGE:
PROVEN

STATE:
VERIFIED

THREE RELATIONSHIPS:
UNKNOWN

ONE CLAIM:
CONTESTED

TWO PROOF OBLIGATIONS:
OPEN

That is not weakness.

It is epistemic integrity.

AN OPEN QUESTION IS BETTER THAN A FALSE ANSWER.


---

XI. ⚓ QUAY PROOF CLOSURE RECORD

The Quay preserves the closure event:

PROOF_OPENED
      ↓
EVIDENCE_ACCUMULATED
      ↓
CHALLENGES_REGISTERED
      ↓
VERIFICATION_COMPLETED
      ↓
PROOF_CLOSED

A later verifier can reconstruct:

WHY WAS THIS CLAIM CONSIDERED PROVEN?

without trusting the current system's memory.


---

XII. 💀 NO RETROACTIVE CERTAINTY

Suppose:

2025:
Claim = Unknown

and in:

2026:
Evidence discovered

Then PALACO must not rewrite history as:

2025:
Claim = Proven

Instead:

2025
CLAIM EXISTED
STATUS = UNKNOWN

2026
EVIDENCE DISCOVERED

2026
VERIFICATION

2026
STATUS = PROVEN

This preserves knowledge-time continuity from R6.27.


---

XIII. 🕰️ TWO HISTORIES

PALACO now formally distinguishes:

Event history

WHAT HAPPENED

Knowledge history

WHEN PALACO ESTABLISHED
WHAT COULD BE PROVEN

Therefore:

EVENT_TIME
≠
KNOWLEDGE_TIME

And:

STATE_HISTORY
≠
EPISTEMIC_HISTORY

Both must remain replayable.


---

XIV. 🌐 FEDERATED PROOF BOUNDARIES

Different Citadels may possess different knowledge:

CITADEL A
────────────
W1 ✓
W2 ✓
W3 ✓

CITADEL B
────────────
W1 ✓
W2 ?
W3 ✓

They must not automatically normalize their knowledge to:

W1 ✓
W2 ✓
W3 ✓

Instead:

FEDERATED KNOWLEDGE
        ↓
A: W2 Proven
B: W2 Unknown
        ↓
RECONCILIATION
        ↓
STATUS EXPLICIT

Plurality of knowledge is preserved until evidence closes the gap.


---

XV. 🏛️ LA PAZ AS A KNOWLEDGE FRONTIER

The La Paz Citadel may therefore report:

LPZ-W18
STATE = VERIFIED

ANCESTRY = PROVEN

FEDERATION = PROVEN

HISTORICAL CLAIMS = 42

PROVEN = 37
CONTESTED = 2
UNKNOWN = 3

This is dramatically more informative than a single:

VALID = TRUE

The Citadel becomes capable of expressing bounded certainty.


---

XVI. 🔐 PROOF BOUNDARY IMMUTABILITY

Once a proof closure is finalized:

PROOF_BOUNDARY

is immutable.

If new evidence later appears:

OLD BOUNDARY
      ↓
NEW EVIDENCE
      ↓
REOPENING EVENT
      ↓
REASSESSMENT
      ↓
NEW BOUNDARY

The original proof state remains historically preserved.

This means:

NEW KNOWLEDGE DOES NOT ERASE OLD KNOWLEDGE STATES.

It supersedes them through documented epistemic evolution.


---

XVII. 🚨 PROOF REGRESSION

A particularly important case:

PROVEN
   ↓
NEW EVIDENCE
   ↓
CHALLENGE
   ↓
REASSESSMENT
   ↓
CONTESTED

PALACO must permit this.

A previous proof can become contested when new evidence invalidates one of its premises.

Therefore:

PROVEN IS NOT SACRED.

It is a historically justified epistemic state.

Its justification must remain challengeable.


---

XVIII. 🧬 PROOF LINEAGE

Every proof state now has ancestry:

CLAIM
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
VERIFICATION
 ↓
PROOF
 ↓
CHALLENGE
 ↓
REASSESSMENT
 ↓
UPDATED PROOF

The system can therefore reconstruct not only:

WHAT WAS PROVEN

but:

WHY WAS IT PROVEN?
WHY DID THAT STATUS CHANGE?


---

XIX. ☄️ PROOF CLOSURE EQUATION

Conceptually:

ProofClosed(C)
=
Evidence(C)
∧ Provenance(C)
∧ Scope(C)
∧ Ruleset(C)
∧ TemporalBinding(C)
∧ Replay(C)
∧ Verification(C)
∧ ChallengeResolution(C)

If any mandatory predicate is false:

ProofClosed(C) = false

No probabilistic averaging.

No confidence score can override a missing constitutional obligation.


---

XX. 🔱 R6.28 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.28-I01
PALACO SHALL explicitly represent the boundary of established constitutional knowledge.

R6.28-I02
Absence of contradictory evidence SHALL NOT constitute proof.

R6.28-I03
Unknown SHALL remain distinct from false.

R6.28-I04
Not-disproven SHALL remain distinct from proven.

R6.28-I05
Claim scope SHALL NOT exceed evidence scope.

R6.28-I06
Every proof claim SHALL have identifiable proof obligations.

R6.28-I07
A proof claim SHALL NOT close while mandatory proof obligations remain unresolved.

R6.28-I08
Proof closure SHALL be independently verifiable.

R6.28-I09
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge an open or previously closed proof.

R6.28-I10
TRIAS SHALL verify proof closure conditions.

R6.28-I11
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT independently close proof obligations.

R6.28-I12
Knowledge-time SHALL remain distinct from event-time.

R6.28-I13
Historical epistemic states SHALL remain immutable records.

R6.28-I14
New evidence SHALL be represented as a new epistemic transition.

R6.28-I15
Previously proven claims SHALL be capable of becoming contested through valid challenge.

R6.28-I16
Proof regression SHALL preserve the historical record of the former proof state.

R6.28-I17
Federated domains SHALL preserve differences in their knowledge boundaries.

R6.28-I18
An open question SHALL NOT be silently converted into a constitutional assumption.

R6.28-I19
No confidence score SHALL substitute for a mandatory proof obligation.

R6.28-I20
PALACO SHALL prefer explicit epistemic incompleteness over fabricated certainty.


---

