XXIV. 🔱 R6.31 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.31-I01
Lineage SHALL NOT by itself confer constitutional authority.

R6.31-I02
Every inherited authority SHALL have a provable source authority.

R6.31-I03
Every transferred authority SHALL be bound to a predecessor watermark.

R6.31-I04
Expired authority SHALL NOT become active solely through succession.

R6.31-I05
Revoked authority SHALL NOT be inherited as active authority.

R6.31-I06
New authority SHALL possess an independent constitutional origin.

R6.31-I07
Technical capability SHALL NOT constitute constitutional authority.

R6.31-I08
Successor authority SHALL be explicitly classified as inherited, new, expired, revoked, excluded, contested, or unknown.

R6.31-I09
Mandatory predecessor obligations SHALL be preserved during succession.

R6.31-I10
Authority transfer SHALL be evidence-bound and provenance-bound.

R6.31-I11
TRIAS SHALL independently verify authority inheritance.

R6.31-I12
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge authority succession.

R6.31-I13
BRAINPOWER SHALL analyze authority mappings but SHALL NOT grant authority.

R6.31-I14
Successor authority SHALL remain temporally bounded.

R6.31-I15
Authority expansion SHALL require explicit proof.

R6.31-I16
Federation membership SHALL NOT automatically transfer constitutional authority.

R6.31-I17
Authority anomalies SHALL remain explicitly represented.

R6.31-I18
Historical authority SHALL remain replayable even after expiration or revocation.

R6.31-I19
Authority and mandatory responsibility SHALL remain constitutionally coupled.

R6.31-I20
A successor SHALL inherit only those powers whose transfer is independently provable.

R6.31-I21
No successor SHALL manufacture ancestral authority from copied state, metadata, identity, or code.

R6.31-I22
Every active successor authority SHALL be traceable to a constitutional proof chain.

R6.31-I23
Unproven successor authority SHALL be blocked from constitutional activation.

R6.31-I24
Successorship SHALL preserve historical truth even when present authority changes.

R6.31-I25
Evolution SHALL NOT constitute an implicit privilege escalation mechanism.


