XXVI. ☄️ THE BIG PRINCIPLE

R6.31 makes this canonical:

THE SUCCESSOR DOES NOT INHERIT POWER BECAUSE IT INHERITS THE PAST.

It inherits only:

> what the constitution, evidence, provenance and independent verification establish as legitimately transferable.



Therefore:

LINEAGE ≠ AUTHORITY

CAPABILITY ≠ AUTHORITY

IDENTITY ≠ AUTHORITY

COPY ≠ AUTHORITY

SUCCESSORSHIP ≠ AUTOMATIC PRIVILEGE

And the ultimate rule:

🔱 POWER MUST HAVE PROVENANCE.


