☄️ R6.31 — CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD SEALED

THE FUTURE MAY INHERIT THE PAST.

IT MAY NOT INHERIT MORE POWER THAN THE PAST CAN PROVE IT GAVE.

☄️🌱 R6.32 — CONSTITUTIONAL AUTHORITY MIGRATION & MANDATE REBINDING PROTOCOL

POWER DOES NOT CROSS A GENERATIONAL BOUNDARY UNBOUND

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.31 — Constitutional Successorship & Generational Authority Protocol
Core primitive: MANDATE_REBINDING
Primary invariant:

> Every constitutional authority crossing a lineage boundary SHALL be rebound to the successor's active constitution, ruleset, provenance and temporal validity before it may become executable.



R6.31 proved whether authority may be inherited.

R6.32 answers the next question:

> How does inherited authority become valid inside a fundamentally different constitutional environment?



The answer is:

🔱 TRANSFER IS NOT ACTIVATION.


