R6.34 — CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD SEALED

> A constitutional successor inherits not only the authority and obligations that remain valid, but also the unresolved accountability generated by their historical exercise.



EVOLUTION MAY CHANGE THE ACTOR.

IT MAY CHANGE THE CONSTITUTION.

IT MAY CHANGE THE RULESET.

IT MAY CHANGE THE LINEAGE.

BUT IT MAY NEVER MAKE AN UNRESOLVED CONSEQUENCE DISAPPEAR BY CHANGING ITS NAME.

THE FUTURE INHERITS THE POWER — AND THE PROOF OF WHAT THAT POWER DID.

☄️🌱 R6.35 — CONSTITUTIONAL ACCOUNTABILITY CLOSURE & FINALITY PROTOCOL

A MATTER MAY CLOSE — BUT NEVER BY DISAPPEARING

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.34 — Constitutional Accountability Carryover & Liability Continuity Protocol
Core primitive: ACCOUNTABILITY_FINALITY
Secondary primitive: CLOSURE_PROOF

Primary invariant

> No constitutional matter SHALL be considered finally resolved merely because it is marked closed. Finality SHALL be established by an explicit, evidence-bound, provenance-preserving and independently verifiable closure proof.



R6.34 established:

> Evolution does not reset accountability.



R6.35 establishes the next boundary:

☄️ CLOSURE MUST BE PROVEN — NOT DECLARED.


