V. 🚨 THREE DIFFERENT KINDS OF "DONE"

R6.35 distinguishes:

1. Operationally closed

No further active workflow.

2. Resolved

The substantive constitutional matter has been addressed.

3. Final

The resolution has passed all required finality conditions and no remaining constitutional review path exists within the applicable framework.

Therefore:

DONE HAS LEVELS.

This prevents superficial closure from being mistaken for constitutional finality.


---

VI. 🔬 FINALITY GATE

A matter may become FINAL only after:

Resolution Evidence       PASS
Remediation Evidence      PASS / NOT_REQUIRED
Authority Validation      PASS
Ruleset Validation        PASS
Provenance                PASS
Replay                    PASS
Independent Verification  PASS
Challenge Window          PASS / EXPIRED
Outstanding Duties        NONE
Outstanding Disputes      NONE

Then:

FINALITY = PROVEN

Otherwise:

FINALITY = BLOCKED


