XXIV. 🔱 R6.35 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.35-I01
Final constitutional closure SHALL require explicit proof.

R6.35-I02
Administrative CLOSED status SHALL NOT by itself constitute constitutional finality.

R6.35-I03
Every finality claim SHALL reference its source accountability matter.

R6.35-I04
Every finality claim SHALL reference the applicable resolution evidence.

R6.35-I05
Finality SHALL be provenance-bound.

R6.35-I06
Finality SHALL be watermark-bound.

R6.35-I07
Finality SHALL be independently verifiable.

R6.35-I08
Finality SHALL be independently replayable.

R6.35-I09
Outstanding mandatory obligations SHALL prevent finality unless explicitly resolved.

R6.35-I10
Outstanding valid challenges SHALL prevent finality where constitutionally applicable.

R6.35-I11
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge finality.

R6.35-I12
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT grant finality.

R6.35-I13
TRIAS SHALL independently verify finality.

R6.35-I14
Finality SHALL NOT erase historical events or accountability records.

R6.35-I15
Reopening SHALL append new history rather than rewrite previous finality.

R6.35-I16
New evidence SHALL be represented as a new constitutional event.

R6.35-I17
Finality SHALL NOT imply metaphysical or absolute infallibility.

R6.35-I18
Federated finality SHALL preserve source-domain finality records.

R6.35-I19
A fabricated finality claim SHALL be explicitly classified as unproven.

R6.35-I20
Finality divergence SHALL identify its first divergent transition.

R6.35-I21
Closure transformations SHALL preserve accountability ancestry.

R6.35-I22
Superseded finality SHALL remain historically discoverable.

R6.35-I23
Temporal passage alone SHALL NOT constitute finality.

R6.35-I24
Finality SHALL remain bounded by the constitution under which it was established.

R6.35-I25
No constitutional matter SHALL disappear merely because it has been marked closed.


