XXVI. ☄️ THE BIG PRINCIPLE

R6.35 makes the final distinction:

A MATTER IS NOT FINISHED BECAUSE THE DATABASE SAYS "CLOSED."

It is finished only when the system can prove:

WHAT happened
WHO acted
UNDER WHICH authority
UNDER WHICH mandate
WHAT obligation applied
WHAT accountability arose
WHAT correction occurred
WHAT evidence supports resolution
WHO independently verified it
WHICH rules determined finality
AND
WHICH watermark records the closure

Therefore:

