R6.37-I17
A precedent SHALL NOT establish its own authority circularly.

R6.37-I18
Federated systems SHALL preserve source-domain precedents.

R6.37-I19
Federated precedent SHALL receive independent provenance.

R6.37-I20
Precedent registration SHALL be watermark-bound.

R6.37-I21
Precedent application SHALL be independently replayable.

R6.37-I22
Historical dissent concerning precedent SHALL remain preserved.

R6.37-I23
New constitutional authority SHALL require an explicit constitutional basis.

R6.37-I24
Historical precedent SHALL inform future reasoning only within constitutionally valid boundaries.

R6.37-I25
No historical record SHALL silently become present authority merely through repetition.


