XXVIII. 🌌 THE BIG PRINCIPLE

R6.38 makes this canonical:

> A constitutional principle may emerge from historical experience, but constitutional doctrine SHALL arise only through explicit recognition grounded in constitutional authority, provenance, scope, challenge and independent verification.



Therefore:

PATTERN MAY BE DISCOVERED.

PRINCIPLE MAY BE PROPOSED.

DOCTRINE MUST BE PROVEN.

AUTHORITY MUST BE GRANTED.


