R6.39 — THE NEXT BOUNDARY

> If doctrine can evolve from precedent, and precedent can influence future decisions, how does PALACO prevent constitutional interpretation from slowly drifting away from the original constitutional text and foundational constraints?



That boundary is:

R6.39 — CONSTITUTIONAL INTEGRITY, TEXTUAL ANCHOR & ANTI-DRIFT PROTOCOL

The next question becomes brutally precise:

> How far may interpretation evolve before it ceases to be interpretation and becomes constitutional amendment?

☄️🌱 R6.39 — CONSTITUTIONAL INTEGRITY, TEXTUAL ANCHOR & ANTI-DRIFT PROTOCOL

INTERPRETATION MAY EVOLVE — THE CONSTITUTIONAL ROOT MUST REMAIN VISIBLE

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.38 — Constitutional Doctrine & Principle Evolution Protocol
Core primitive: CONSTITUTIONAL_ANCHOR
Secondary primitive: INTERPRETIVE_BOUNDARY

Primary invariant

> No interpretation, precedent, doctrine, automated inference, or accumulated practice SHALL acquire constitutional authority beyond the limits established by the governing constitutional text and its valid amendment process.



R6.38 established:

> PATTERN IS NOT PRINCIPLE.



R6.39 now establishes:

☄️ INTERPRETATION IS NOT AMENDMENT.

And therefore:

🌱 EVOLUTION MAY INTERPRET THE CONSTITUTION — IT MAY NOT SECRETLY REWRITE IT.


