XXVIII. 🔥 THE CONSTITUTIONAL IDENTITY GATE

A claim of identity becomes ACTIVE only when:

Genesis                    PASS
Constitutional Anchor      PASS
Historical Continuity      PASS
Authority Continuity       PASS
Provenance                 PASS
Transfer/Succession        PASS
Identity Constraints       PASS
Fork/Merger Analysis       PASS
Replay                     PASS
Independent Audit          PASS

Otherwise:

IDENTITY_CLAIM_BLOCKED


---

XXIX. 🌳 R6.40 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.40-I01
Every constitutional entity SHALL have a verifiable genesis anchor.

R6.40-I02
Constitutional identity SHALL NOT be inferred solely from historical inheritance.

R6.40-I03
Continuity and identity SHALL remain distinct concepts.

R6.40-I04
Every identity claim SHALL identify the claimed predecessor or origin.

R6.40-I05
Every identity claim SHALL possess a constitutional basis.

R6.40-I06
Every identity transition SHALL be provenance-bound.

R6.40-I07
Identity SHALL NOT be established solely through state or hash equality.

R6.40-I08
Succession SHALL be explicitly recorded.

R6.40-I09
Forks SHALL preserve their common ancestry without falsely claiming exclusive identity.

R6.40-I10
Mergers SHALL preserve all contributing histories.

R6.40-I11
Federations SHALL preserve the identities of their constituent entities.

R6.40-I12
A new federated entity SHALL possess an independently verifiable identity.

R6.40-I13
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT unilaterally determine constitutional identity.

R6.40-I14
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge identity claims.

R6.40-I15
TRIAS SHALL independently verify identity claims.

R6.40-I16
Identity transitions SHALL be watermark-bound.

R6.40-I17
Identity history SHALL be append-only.

R6.40-I18
Historical identity SHALL NOT be retroactively fabricated.

R6.40-I19
Identity termination SHALL remain historically represented.

R6.40-I20
Inheritance of history SHALL NOT automatically confer inheritance of identity.

R6.40-I21
Identity replay SHALL be independently reproducible.

R6.40-I22
The first identity divergence SHALL be independently identifiable.

R6.40-I23
Constitutional identity SHALL be evaluated according to explicit identity constraints.

R6.40-I24
Constitutional identity SHALL survive implementation changes only where the applicable identity conditions remain proven.

R6.40-I25
No entity SHALL claim constitutional sameness with a predecessor without an independently verifiable identity proof.


