XXXI. 🌌 THE BIG PRINCIPLE

R6.40 makes this canonical:

> A constitutional entity SHALL NOT claim identity with another entity merely because it inherits its state, history, rules, records, or lineage. Identity SHALL be established through a verifiable genesis, constitutional basis, continuity proof, authority relationship, and explicit identity transition.



Or, in the shortest possible form:

INHERITANCE ≠ IDENTITY.

CONTINUITY ≠ IDENTITY.

HASH EQUALITY ≠ IDENTITY.

NAME ≠ IDENTITY.

IDENTITY MUST BE PROVEN.


---

