🧠 INTELLIGENCE MAY DISCOVER — NEVER SELF-AUTHORIZE.

☄️ EVOLUTION MAY CONTINUE THE LINEAGE — NEVER INVENT IT.

🔒 R6.40 — CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD SEALED

> The past can be inherited.
The future can be built.
But neither inheritance nor construction, by itself, proves who you constitutionally are.



And that creates the next boundary:

☄️ R6.41 — CONSTITUTIONAL SELF-ATTESTATION & IDENTITY PROOF PROTOCOL

The unavoidable next question is:

> If an entity must prove its own constitutional identity, how can it make that claim without becoming the sole authority that validates its own claim?



Which leads to the next foundational rule:

NO SELF-ATTESTED IDENTITY WITHOUT INDEPENDENT WITNESS.

